2012-09-30 18:59:21		manage windows
2012-09-30 18:59:21		         list: list opened windows (without argument, this list is displayed)
2012-09-30 18:59:21		           -1: jump to previous window
2012-09-30 18:59:21		           +1: jump to next window
2012-09-30 18:59:21		           b#: jump to next window displaying buffer number #
2012-09-30 18:59:21		           up: switch to window above current one
2012-09-30 18:59:21		         down: switch to window below current one
2012-09-30 18:59:21		         left: switch to window on the left
2012-09-30 18:59:21		        right: switch to window on the right
2012-09-30 18:59:21		       number: window number (see /window list)
2012-09-30 18:59:21		       splith: split current window horizontally
2012-09-30 18:59:21		       splitv: split current window vertically
2012-09-30 18:59:21		       resize: resize window size, new size is <pct> percentage of parent window
2012-09-30 18:59:21		      balance: balance the sizes of all windows
2012-09-30 18:59:21		        merge: merge window with another (all = keep only one window)
2012-09-30 18:59:21		      page_up: scroll one page up
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    page_down: scroll one page down
2012-09-30 18:59:21		      refresh: refresh screen
2012-09-30 18:59:21		       scroll: scroll a number of lines (+/-N) or with time: s=seconds, m=minutes, h=hours, d=days, M=months, y=years
2012-09-30 18:59:21		 scroll_horiz: scroll horizontally a number of columns (+/-N) or percentage of window size (this scrolling is possible only on buffers with free content)
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    scroll_up: scroll a few lines up
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  scroll_down: scroll a few lines down
2012-09-30 18:59:21		   scroll_top: scroll to top of buffer
2012-09-30 18:59:21		scroll_bottom: scroll to bottom of buffer
2012-09-30 18:59:21		scroll_previous_highlight: scroll to previous highlight
2012-09-30 18:59:21		scroll_next_highlight: scroll to next highlight
2012-09-30 18:59:21		scroll_unread: scroll to unread marker
2012-09-30 18:59:21		         swap: swap buffers of two windows (with optional direction for target window)
2012-09-30 18:59:21		         zoom: zoom on window
2012-09-30 18:59:21		For splith and splitv, pct is a percentage which represents size of new window, computed with current window as size reference. For example 25 means create a new window with size = current_size / 4
2012-09-30 18:59:21		Examples:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  jump to window displaying buffer #1:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    /window b1
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  scroll 2 lines up:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    /window scroll -2
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  scroll 2 days up:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    /window scroll -2d
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  scroll to beginning of current day:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    /window scroll -d
2012-09-30 18:59:21		  zoom on window #2:
2012-09-30 18:59:21		    /window zoom -window 2
